    "payload": {
      "content": "When reviewing theoretical machine learning papers (e.g., on self-supervised learning dynamics) for the POL dimension, prioritize checking for double-blind anonymity violations (POL-ANO) such as explicit author names, affiliations, or email addresses in the header, which are common in early drafts. Additionally, verify the presence of a 'Broader Impact' or 'Ethical Considerations' section (POL-IMP), as its absence is a frequent weakness even in purely theoretical works. For data usage (POL-DAT), standard public benchmarks like CIFAR-10 and STL-10 are generally compliant with privacy and licensing regulations, serving as a strength. Ensure that ethical concerns (POL-ETH) are assessed based on the general applicability of the method, noting that general-purpose optimization techniques typically lack specific fairness or bias risks unless applied to sensitive domains.",
      "reviewer_dimension": "POL",
      "source": "6d614eef79f7034d55f0399254bda81c5e1b62b3a70a113687d37fe352cae559",
      "topic": "POL Review: Double-blind violations and missing broader impact statements in theoretical SSL papers"
